        "question_title": "A rectangle has fixed area \\(48\\,\\mathrm{cm^2}\\) and length \\(x\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\), where \\(x>0\\). What is the minimum possible perimeter?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The breadth is \\(b=\\frac{48}{x}\\). Thus \\(P=2\\left(x+\\frac{48}{x}\\right)\\). By AM-GM, \\(x+\\frac{48}{x}\\ge 2\\sqrt{48}=8\\sqrt{3}\\), so \\(P_{\\min}=16\\sqrt{3}\\,\\mathrm{cm}\\).",
